Package: scUmaper
Type: Package
Title: Single Cell Utility Matrices Processing Engine in R
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(person(given="Xushun",family="Guo",role="aut",email="guoxsh3@mail3.sysu.edu.cn"),
  person(given="Jinzhe",family="Huang",role="aut"),
  person(given="Gaoshi",family="Zhou",role=c("aut","cre"),email="zhougshi@mail3.sysu.edu.cn"))
Maintainer: Gaoshi Zhou <zhougshi@mail3.sysu.edu.cn>
Description: A streamlined single-cell transcriptomics processing pipeline designed for 
    researchers with limited bioinformatics experience. 'scUmaper' automatically removes 
    heterotypic doublets and annotates cell clusters with high reliability by leveraging 
    known biological markers. It directly accepts raw gene expression matrices from 10x 
    Genomics (human or mouse tissues), bypassing intermediate manual steps to reduce 
    potential analytical errors. Optionally, users can input pre-processed Seurat 
    objects and define custom marker gene lists for tailored cell-type annotation.
